methods.explanation:
Evaluate the inner square roots first, because their values determine the numbers under the outer radicals. Since \(\sqrt{81}=9\) and \(\sqrt{16}=4\),
\[
\frac{\sqrt{16\sqrt{81}}}{\sqrt{81\sqrt{16}}}
=\frac{\sqrt{16\cdot9}}{\sqrt{81\cdot4}}
=\frac{\sqrt{144}}{\sqrt{324}}
=\frac{12}{18}
=\boxed{\frac23}.
\]
The radical symbol gives the nonnegative square root, and the denominator is \(18>0\). The answer is choice \(\mathrm{B}\).
